WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.270
Choosing a home is one of the biggest
decisions we make.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.210
Two in five Australians have experienced a
mental health condition.

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.930
And where we live shapes everyday life.

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.150
Yet most listings only tell you about the
property, not the neighbourhood around it.

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.960
Microburbs Facts is a Chrome extension

6
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.790
that sits beside the property listings
you already browse.

7
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.020
Open a listing and it confirms the
address,

8
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.560
then brings the local facts together in
one panel.

9
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.490
No copying addresses into another site.

10
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.750
Start with what matters day to day.

11
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.540
The Neighbourhood Wellbeing Index

12
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.550
scores the suburb out of 100,
calculated from five indicators.

13
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.650
Here Surry Hills scores 49.

14
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.730
Open the indicators to see what's driving
the score,

15
00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.250
so you can weigh the trade-offs,

16
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.380
not just a number.

17
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.310
It's a neighbourhood measure, not a
clinical assessment.

18
00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:58.000
Everyday living shows what's within reach,
using straight-line distances.

19
00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.140
This home is about 130 metres from Surry
Hills Station,

20
00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:06.460
20 metres from Tudor Street Reserve, and a
short walk to the local grocer.

21
00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.540
Where data isn't available yet, Microburbs
says so, rather than guessing.

22
00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.070
Renting?

23
00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.890
Microburbs shows the latest advertised
rent where it's on record

24
00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.520
and lets you type in the asking rent to
see how it compares.

25
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:24.310
Buying?

26
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:28.920
Switch tabs for an estimated value with
its range and confidence,

27
00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:34.480
the last sale, and recent comparable sales
nearby, with 50 more a tap away.

28
00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:37.950
Then check planning and zoning at the
address

29
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.920
and overlays like flooding and bushfire.

30
00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.100
Every figure is labelled for what it is.

31
00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.860
A model estimate, not a formal appraisal.

32
00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.740
Homes are rarely chosen alone.

33
00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.990
Save a property to your notes,
which stay in your browser,

34
00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.460
and share it with the people you live with
so you can decide together.

35
00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:01.920
And follow Microburbs for suburb insights
and market updates.

36
00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:04.920
Want the detail behind a number?

37
00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.620
Open sources and full property report to
see where each figure comes from.

38
00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.280
Microburbs only shows what it can source
and tells you when something's missing.

39
00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.910
Because you're not just choosing a
property,

40
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.450
you're choosing where life happens.

41
00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.530
Microburbs. Find the facts, find your fit.
